hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1706","Narrated to us 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-'Ala', narrated to us Sufyan, narrated to us 'Amr—he is Ibn Dinar—who informed me Abu Ma'bad, on the authority of Ibn 'Abbas (RA), who said:\n*\I used to recognize the conclusion of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)'s prayer by the Takbir.\""*\n\n**CHAPTER:**"""""
"1707","**\nNarrated to us Al-Hasan ibn Mahdī: Narrated to us ‘Abd al-Razzāq: Narrated to us Ibn Jurayj: Narrated to me ‘Amr ibn Dīnār: That Abū Ma‘bad informed him, on the authority of Ibn ‘Abbās (RA), that he said:\n\n*\Indeed"","" raising the voice with remembrance when departing from the prescribed prayer was done during the time of the Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ).\""*\n\nIbn ‘Abbās (RA) said: *\""I knew when they had finished [the prayer] by that [i.e."","" by hearing them raise their voices with remembrance].\""*"""""
